{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_5",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_9",
      "quote": "Studies were included if they met the following criteria: (1) clinical trials and observational studies that examine the use of laryngoscopes with tracheal tube introducers and/",
      "reason": "The manuscript begins to specify study characteristics (designs: clinical trials and observational studies) but the inclusion criteria text is truncated and does not present a complete list of eligibility characteristics (settings, follow-up requirements, full question-framework components are not fully reported in the retrieved evidence)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": \"We conducted a search on the 2nd of March 2021 across the following databases: PubMed, Embase (Ovid) and the Cochrane Central Register of Controlled Trials (CENTRAL). ... The search terms used were as follows: 'Prehospital' AND ('Tracheal tube introducer' OR 'Gum elastic bougie' OR 'Flexible tip bougie' OR 'Eschmann tracheal tube introducer' OR 'Frova introducer' OR 'Stylet'). No publication date limitations were set.\",
      "reason": "The paper reports report-related criteria such as search date, databases searched, search terms, and that no publication date limits were applied, but it does not specify other report characteristics (e.g., language restrictions or publication/report status) in the retrieved evidence."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_10",
      "quote": "Five full-text articles were excluded, two reported the use of a bougie/stylet in an exchange manoeuvre, one reported the use of a stylet without laryngoscope and two did not report bougie/stylet efficacy outcomes at all.",
      "reason": "The study selection description explicitly lists exclusion reasons including studies excluded because they did not report the efficacy outcomes, thereby distinguishing at least exclusion due to non-reporting of outcomes."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_13",
      "quote": \"Two studies [20, 21] were included in our meta-analysis of bougie versus stylet first pass ETI success for prehospital studies without video technology (Fig. 3)... Two studies [14, 15] were included in our meta-analysis of bougie versus stylet first pass ETI success for prehospital studies with video technology (Fig. 4). ... Overall, the summary estimate of prehospital ETI Endotracheal intubation studies with video technology showed a statistically significant difference between devices for first pass ETI success, favouring the use of a bougie (RR 1.15, CI 1.10-1.21, p < 0.00001).\"",
      "reason": "The manuscript specifies how studies were grouped for syntheses (e.g., prehospital vs simulation, with video technology vs without, and bougie versus stylet comparisons) and links these groups to the meta-analyses and outcomes reported."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_15",
      "quote": \"This review aimed to focus exclusively on the prehospital efficacy of these devices to guide the practice of prehospital personnel in their unique setting, thus inclusion of hospital-based RCTs was deemed inappropriate.\",
      "reason": "The authors provide a rationale for notable eligibility restrictions, specifically explaining why hospital-based RCTs were excluded (to focus exclusively on prehospital efficacy)."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 80
}

